meta {
  name: 14 - Issues Include Archived
  type: graphql
  seq: 14
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}
  body: graphql
  auth: inherit
}

body:graphql {
  query IssuesIncludeArchived {
    liveOnly: issues(first: 250, orderBy: updatedAt) {
      nodes { id archivedAt updatedAt }
      pageInfo { hasNextPage }
    }
    withArchived: issues(first: 250, includeArchived: true, orderBy: updatedAt) {
      nodes { id archivedAt updatedAt }
      pageInfo { hasNextPage }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Reference: https://linear.app/developers/graphql

  The silent-data-loss probe for this stream. Linear's default hides a whole partition:
  "Archived resources are hidden by default from the paginated responses. They can be
  included by passing optional `includeArchived: true` as a query parameter for
  pagination."

  Archival is how deletion is normally expressed in Linear's UI, so a connector that omits
  `includeArchived` does not merely miss archived rows — it makes archival INVISIBLE. A
  record that gets archived simply stops appearing in incremental sweeps, and the
  downstream collection keeps serving a stale live-looking copy forever, with no tombstone
  and no signal that anything happened. That is silent data loss in the exact sense the
  verification rules are about.

  `03 - Introspect Entity Types` confirmed `archivedAt: DateTime` (nullable) is exposed on
  all four cluster types, so with `includeArchived: true` the archived partition is
  self-identifying downstream: `archivedAt != null` IS the tombstone. No separate deletion
  mechanism is needed.

  Recommendation, therefore: set `includeArchived: true` on ALL FOUR cluster streams,
  unconditionally, and always select `archivedAt`.

  **Limitation / observed finding — RESOLVED, and it is a VERIFIED NEGATIVE.**

  Two runs, before and after `Seeding/D2 - Archive Issue`:

  - **2026-07-30 (pre-seed, the saved example below):** zero archived records existed, so
    `liveOnly` and `withArchived` both returned the same 4 rows, all `archivedAt: null`.
    Proved only that the argument is accepted.
  - **2026-08-04 (post-seed, EST-2 archived):** `withArchived` -> 4 rows, `liveOnly` -> 3.
    `includeArchived: true` genuinely works, and the default genuinely hides the partition.

  **But the load-bearing assumption FAILED. Archiving does NOT bump `updatedAt`:**

  | EST-2 | before | after `issueArchive` |
  |---|---|---|
  | `updatedAt` | `2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z` | **unchanged** |
  | `archivedAt` | `null` | `2026-08-04T18:13:09.393Z` |
  | visible by default | yes | no |

  So an `updatedAt`-cursored incremental sweep will **never** re-emit an archived record,
  and `includeArchived: true` buys incremental sync **nothing on its own** — the row is
  merely eligible to appear, and nothing ever asks for it again. Had the connector shipped
  on the original assumption, deleted records would sit in destination tables looking live,
  indefinitely.

  Ordinary field mutations DO bump `updatedAt` (verified via `Seeding/D1` on EST-1:
  `…03.808Z` -> `2026-08-04T18:12:51.985Z`). It is specifically archival that does not.

  `includeArchived: true` is still REQUIRED on every request in this cluster — without it
  archived rows cannot be retrieved by any means. It is simply not SUFFICIENT.

  What replaces the original design:
  - **Issues** — a second, independently-cursored pass on `filter.archivedAt.gt`. See
    `15 - Issues Archival Sweep`.
  - **Projects / Initiatives / Labels** — no `archivedAt` filter exists on their filter
    types, so archival is not incrementally detectable at all. See
    `08 - Archival Capability Matrix`.
}

example {
  name: 200 — withArchived=4 / liveOnly=3; updatedAt NOT bumped by archive

  request: {
    url: https://api.linear.app/graphql
    method: POST
    mode: graphql

    body:graphql: {
      query IssuesIncludeArchived {
        liveOnly: issues(first: 250, orderBy: updatedAt) {
          nodes { id archivedAt updatedAt }
          pageInfo { hasNextPage }
        }
        withArchived: issues(first: 250, includeArchived: true, orderBy: updatedAt) {
          nodes { id archivedAt updatedAt }
          pageInfo { hasNextPage }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    headers: {
      x-complexity: 7
      x-ratelimit-requests-limit: 2500
      x-ratelimit-requests-remaining: 2487
      x-ratelimit-complexity-limit: 3000000
      x-ratelimit-complexity-remaining: 2999989
    }

    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }

    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "liveOnly": {
              "count": 3,
              "rows": [
                {
                  "id": "4937bc7e-6bda-4612-9a80-3fbaaec872d9",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-08-04T18:12:51.985Z",
                  "archivedAt": null
                },
                {
                  "id": "adbc7deb-6607-4f39-ade2-c23268dc3ec7",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z",
                  "archivedAt": null
                },
                {
                  "id": "86eeb50c-332c-46a7-bebf-a0b67dc346bf",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z",
                  "archivedAt": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "withArchived": {
              "count": 4,
              "rows": [
                {
                  "id": "4937bc7e-6bda-4612-9a80-3fbaaec872d9",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-08-04T18:12:51.985Z",
                  "archivedAt": null
                },
                {
                  "id": "adbc7deb-6607-4f39-ade2-c23268dc3ec7",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z",
                  "archivedAt": null
                },
                {
                  "id": "86eeb50c-332c-46a7-bebf-a0b67dc346bf",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z",
                  "archivedAt": null
                },
                {
                  "id": "431c9f95-fe23-44cb-9391-f4880c51bede",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z",
                  "archivedAt": "2026-08-04T18:13:09.393Z"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
